  "2026-11-04T23:21:11.257Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof in a disposable non-git source copy: baseline two regressions passed (exit 0); moving only the resource guard into the controller callback failed (exit 1, AssertionError) because a real live competing lease returned loop_controller_active instead of process_budget_exhausted; removing only the guard failed the same regression; reverting only the approval documentation failed its contract test. Restored implementation and docs passed 2/2 (exit 0). docs/proposer-revert-evidence.json records all cases. Strengthened exact-budget controller test passed with five fits, ten jobs, zero-token allowance, replay, six retained promotion slots and competing-search refusal. Linked pm test passed 2/2 using pm_context_mode=none and workspace_context_mode=snapshot; isolated mode has no source files, so snapshot is required."
  "2026-11-04T23:27:54.037Z",codex-agent,"Release-gate follow-up from prior Node 22 CI: 1483/1483 tests passed but V8 reported 99.99% branch coverage, naming index.ts:5689. A direct raw-V8 probe isolated a zero-count range containing only whitespace between a catch that always throws and its finally block; both real error branches executed. Separated proposer CLI error translation from outer signal cleanup with nested try/catch and outer finally, preserving all behavior. A minimal V8 control reproduces the original whitespace range and confirms this conventional layout removes it. Stopped the superseded local npm gate after this source edit; restart both complete gates on finalized source, with unchanged thresholds. Local strict health still has no integrity/history drift but retains existing ambient extension version skew and legacy provenance advisory; no history repair or dependency bump."
