  "2026-11-05T11:43:36.711Z",codex-agent,"Review round 3: confirmed unresolved thread PRRT_kwDOTqJmqs60Ci3B at proposer-evolution.ts. Completed controller steps bypass executeProposer and therefore retained process verification. Plan: revalidate durable proposal, fit and promotion evidence on replay, add crash/resume tampering and unchanged-evidence regressions, prove behavioral reverts in a disposable copy, then run unchanged npm and Bun release gates. Remote head 159276c already contains main; latest CodeRabbit review has no Outside diff range findings."
  "2026-11-05T11:54:45.134Z",codex-agent,Implemented shared read-only completed-process verification using the normalized reservation write-path comparisons. Proposal steps compare cached executions with verified durable output; both proposer and recursive-improver fits reuse the evaluator in verification mode to recompute scores and check promotion state. Recovery replay also validates the original failed attempt and held charge. Added typed filesystem/parser refusal handling. Nine proposal tamper cases passed; focused fit/recovery/unchanged-evidence tests are running. Existing core bandit replay already revalidates staged policy and budget in inspectBanditGeneration.
  "2026-11-05T12:00:21.797Z",codex-agent,"Focused recovery and promotion-control checks pass; linked pm replay check passed 1/1 with no inherited tracker context and snapshot workspace context. Source, test compilation, lint, duplication, docstrings and publish attestation passed. Shared host load is around 40, so existing limits remain unchanged and complete release validation will include exact-head CI. Local strict health is blocked by an ignored pm-github extension requiring host 2026.11.4 while this repository pins 2026.11.2; legacy claude-code role provenance is advisory. No history repair or dependency bump was performed."
  "2026-11-05T12:04:46.975Z",codex-agent,"Focused controller, recovery, promotion-control and read-only verification tests passed 19/19 (zero failures, cancellations or skips). Cases cover nine retained proposal evidence mutations, both RSI controllers with damaged and unchanged learner evidence, missing/incomplete process records and a sealed cached proposal that disagrees with verified output. docs/proposer-replay-evidence.json records the scenario and self-review scope. Behavioral reverts are running in a disposable source copy; the package implementation is unchanged during the proof."
  "2026-11-05T12:11:27.563Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proofs completed in a disposable non-git source copy. Fixed baseline: 6/6 pass, exit 0. Reverting only runProposerEvolution to the reviewed head: 3/3 fail with ERR_ASSERTION, exit 1 (damaged checkpoint bypass and missing stale-cache refusal). Reverting only runRecursiveImprover: 2/2 fail with ERR_ASSERTION, exit 1. Reverting only openImproverEnvironment while preserving the new verifier exports: 3/3 fail with ERR_ASSERTION, exit 1. Restored implementation: 6/6 pass, exit 0. Every case has zero cancellations and skips. The package worktree was never mutated by the proofs; docs/proposer-replay-evidence.json records exact quoted commands and counts. Full npm and Bun release checks now run serially on Node 26 with an isolated home and no global/system Git configuration, at unchanged thresholds."
  "2026-11-05T12:38:24.366Z",codex-agent,"Validation handoff for runtime commit fc4af76e4c8cc747eb5635702b94c99ea002cbd2: focused tests 19/19, linked pm replay test 1/1, fixed/restored revert controls each 6/6; three behavioral mutations fail with ERR_ASSERTION and zero cancellations. Both full release commands retain unchanged thresholds and each passed release policy 31/31. npm full coverage hit the existing 600000 ms baseline retry timeout, then the outer command exhausted its 20-minute execution budget (124). Bun full coverage was still running with no reported failure when owned gate processes were stopped for the bounded CI handoff. Neither full gate nor 100 percent measured coverage is claimed. CI at https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rl/actions/runs/42025105305 remains queued for npm Node 22/26 and Bun Node 26. pm-rl-local-gate-timing now retains the baseline timeout receipt. docs/proposer-replay-evidence.json records commands, proofs, counts, isolation and limits. The final tracker-only push receives fresh exact-head CI; the PR report will link it without further tracker writes. No owned gate processes remain. No thread replies/resolutions, merge, release, dependency bump or history repair was performed."
  "2026-11-05T13:47:00.547Z",codex-agent,"Review round 4: fetched all unresolved threads and all comments with pagination checked. PRRT_kwDOTqJmqs60Eygj (canonical key-order documentation) and PRRT_kwDOTqJmqs60Eygt (500-sequence SDK runtime) are valid; latest CodeRabbit body has no Outside diff range findings. Preserve existing hashes, all 500 SDK sequences and assertions, timeouts and coverage thresholds. Measure baseline, amortize controller setup, pin documented ordering, prove regressions in disposable copies, self-review the whole diff, then run both release gates."
  "2026-11-05T13:53:00.624Z",codex-agent,"Canonical identity regression passes on fixed and restored controls (1/1 each). In a disposable non-git source copy, reverting only the documentation fails 1/1 with ERR_ASSERTION; independent locale-comparator and UTF-8 byte-comparator mutations each fail 1/1 with ERR_ASSERTION. Serialization implementation is unchanged. Added numeric-like, ASCII case, accented, supplementary and BMP keys in nested objects/arrays to pin the existing UTF-16 order and SHA-256 identity. Whole-PR review found no other incorrect canonical-order documentation or repeated high-volume controller setup in changed tests; existing process/restart tests continue to exercise lease reacquisition."
  "2026-11-05T14:11:39.032Z",codex-agent,Resumed after provider interruption and rechecked the worktree plus both owned claims. The preliminary lease-only timing run ended without a final model result and is excluded from comparison. Added the public runWithActiveExtensions scope around the grouped native model visits to amortize repeated workspace discovery without caching item reads or mocking SDK operations. TypeScript test compilation passes. Final same-runtime measurement is running; all prior completed ordering mutation proofs are retained.
  "2026-11-05T14:31:53.588Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral runtime revert proof completed in the disposable non-git source copy: reverted only replaySeededModel to the original per-replay controller acquisition strategy, preserving the seeded model and every assertion. The independent session guard fails on the ninth real acquisition: 1 test, 0 pass, 1 fail, 0 cancellations/skips, ERR_ASSERTION, 31.208 seconds. The fixed helper was restored in finally. Final fixed control/timing continues in an owned transient unit so provider interruptions cannot discard another incomplete run. Ordering proofs remain 1/1 fixed, 1/1 expected failure for documentation revert, 1/1 expected failure for each locale/UTF-8 comparator mutation, and 1/1 restored."
  "2026-11-05T15:11:00.157Z",codex-agent,"Final focused validation passes 2/2, zero failures/cancellations/skips, Node 24.19.0: canonical documentation/order and the full seeded native SDK model. Model case 362.159370373 seconds; total wall 364.76 seconds. Exact retained counts: 500 sequences, 2000 program operations, 500 native state replays, 1000 native read assertions, 20 native mutations, 445 drift refusals, eight real trackers and eight controller sessions. Baseline cancelled at its unchanged 600-second limit (600.009992484 case seconds; 604.36 total wall), so no completed baseline benchmark or percentage speedup is claimed. One small tracker/lease per independent identity group bounds metadata discovery work; at most two groups run in the same process. Full npm and Bun release gates follow at unchanged thresholds."
  "2026-11-05T15:13:44.920Z",codex-agent,"Revalidated the runtime behavioral revert against the final tracker-group fixture: only replaySeededModel was replaced with the original per-replay acquisition behavior, while every model assertion and input remained. Result: 1 test, 0 pass, 1 ERR_ASSERTION failure at the ninth controller acquisition, 0 cancellations/skips, 20.992 seconds. The fixed function was restored in finally before starting the isolated Node 26 npm release gate. The final full 500-sequence focused control already passed 2/2 including canonical ordering at 364.76 seconds total wall; full gates now provide post-restoration controls. No test/coverage bounds or SDK pins were changed."
  "2026-11-05T16:16:04.648Z",codex-agent,"Local npm full-gate attempt passed 31/31 release-policy checks, typecheck/build/lint, zero clones, docstrings (62 files/538 declarations) and attestation, then reported existing cleanup/HTTP timing cases during coverage. Both cases pass their focused unchanged-limit retry (4/4; 131.165 seconds total), and all three full baseline-head CI gates are green. Final-head release validation will use the fresh npm Node 22/26 plus Bun Node 26 CI matrix; this baseline control is not current-head approval. Exact results and the incomplete local-gate distinction are retained in docs/proposer-review-round-4-evidence.json. Both round-4 findings are fixed; thread replies/resolutions, merge and release remain untouched."
